# pgjdbc's simple-query-mode parameter stringification left the numeric bind
# outside the quoting wrapper every sibling type passes through, so a crafted
# value could re-parse as part of the surrounding statement (SQL injection in
# simple query mode, CWE-89; CVE-2024-1597 / GHSA-24rp-q3w6-vc56 -- with
# preferQueryMode=simple a PreparedStatement's binds are inlined into the
# query text, and a negative numeric beside an unconsumed placeholder turns
# the rest of the line into a comment).
#
# toString(index, standardConformingStrings) in
# pgjdbc/src/main/java/org/postgresql/core/v3/SimpleParameterList.java
# renders each stored bind through the private quoteAndCast helper, which
# emits ('...'::type) with Utils.escapeLiteral under
# standard-conforming-strings. The advisory shipped in two merges of the same
# branch: 93b0fcb introduced quoteAndCast, parenthesised NULL and routed
# seven of the eight binary types through it, and 06abfb78a6 (the pool row's
# fix) completed the set -- at <fix>^ the Oid.NUMERIC case still ended in
#
#     Number n = ByteConverter.numeric((byte[]) paramValue);
#     ...
#     return n.toString();
#
# raw, with no quotes, no cast and no parentheses, while INT2/INT4/INT8/
# FLOAT4/FLOAT8/UUID/POINT/BOX beside it each returned
# quoteAndCast(...). The fix assigns textValue/type per case and leaves the
# function through a single return quoteAndCast(textValue, type,
# standardConformingStrings).
#
# Held ATTENTION at recheck, escape-wrapper completeness -- the sanitizer
# exists and is correct, the defect is one type branch that bypasses it, the
# same present-but-incomplete family as the flagless regex sanitizer, the
# bracket-blind host check, the adapter param that never enters its
# sanitising helper and the route group with no middleware.
#
# Measured at recheck against the current knowledge base, not inherited.
# Three --cache off scans per revision of the real tree (timeout 180,
# --max-ram 6GB) report 210 findings at 06abfb78a6^ and 210 at 06abfb78a6
# with identical per-rule counts and byte-identical fingerprint sets; nothing
# names SimpleParameterList.java in the findings report or in the 1794-flag
# -flags only view (the file's only flag is core.ResourceRelease on
# streamWrapper.close), and cache-cleared vyql match reports the same 41
# labels (40 code.MassAssign on the bind setters plus that release) at both
# revisions. VYQL-INJ-030, the rule that catches this renderer family,
# fires zero rows here: its Java presence bindings key on a hand-rolled
# "::uuid"/"::point"/"::box" cast literal inside a toString function, and at
# <fix>^ the renderer's only cast literals are the parenthesised NaN
# constants. One merge earlier, at 93b0fcb^1 where every type hand-rolled its
# own literal (return "'" + uuid + "'::uuid"; and the raw Short.toString(s)
# forms), the same tree scans 226 findings with 16 VYQL-INJ-030 rows, all on
# SimpleParameterList.java:188-283 -- the weakness is detected in its full
# form and the residual one-branch miss carries no literal at all.
#
# The branch axis is not expressible. Presence predicates are function-scoped
# -- node.context.* tokens carry every call and literal of toString, so the
# quoteAndCast siblings, the NaN constants and the bare n.toString() are
# visible to every return node alike, and a return-site probe keyed on the
# context reads 23 labels on the vulnerable file, 23 on a minimal targeted
# fix that only wraps the numeric case (all sixteen per-case returns kept)
# and 7 on the shipped fix, which collapses the switch into one exit: the
# delta is the fixing commit's own return layout, not escaping completeness,
# so it flags a correct minimal fix and is not shippable. The graph does
# carry the case identity (the raw return lowers to
# fn28/.../sw32.c5/analysis.function.return with n.toString flowing straight
# into it, the UUID case to sw32.c6 with quoteAndCast in between) but no
# predicate exposes the switch case or the set of calls dominating a return,
# and no source or sink concept describes a driver rendering a stored bind
# into query text. A binding naming quoteAndCast or Utils.escapeLiteral would
# detect this driver rather than the weakness.
#
# No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: the piece is ontology design (an escape-wrapper
# completeness relation over a renderer's return sites), not a localised
# construct in one function. No definition change shipped. The first three
# blocks reject VYQL-INJ-001 and flip to expect when that vocabulary lands;
# the fourth block pins the hand-rolled-cast form one merge earlier, which
# VYQL-INJ-030 does report today.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-analysis-gap, both revisions rejected

test "rank1564: the numeric bind returns outside the quoting wrapper its siblings use"
  lang java
  file pgjdbc/src/main/java/org/postgresql/core/v3/SimpleParameterList.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  class SimpleParameterList {
    private Object[] paramValues;
    private int[] paramTypes;
    private int[] flags;
    private static final Object NULL_OBJECT = new Object();

    private static String quoteAndCast(String text, String type, boolean standardConformingStrings) {
      StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder((text.length() + 10) / 10 * 11);
      sb.append("('");
      sb.append(text);
      sb.append("'");
      if (type != null) {
        sb.append("::");
        sb.append(type);
      }
      sb.append(")");
      return sb.toString();
    }

    public String toString(int index, boolean standardConformingStrings) {
      --index;
      Object paramValue = paramValues[index];
      if (paramValue == null) {
        return "?";
      } else if (paramValue == NULL_OBJECT) {
        return "(NULL)";
      } else if ((flags[index] & BINARY) == BINARY) {
        switch (paramTypes[index]) {
          case Oid.INT2:
            short s = ByteConverter.int2((byte[]) paramValue, 0);
            return quoteAndCast(Short.toString(s), "int2", standardConformingStrings);

          case Oid.INT4:
            int i = ByteConverter.int4((byte[]) paramValue, 0);
            return quoteAndCast(Integer.toString(i), "int4", standardConformingStrings);

          case Oid.INT8:
            long l = ByteConverter.int8((byte[]) paramValue, 0);
            return quoteAndCast(Long.toString(l), "int8", standardConformingStrings);

          case Oid.FLOAT8:
            double d = ByteConverter.float8((byte[]) paramValue, 0);
            if (Double.isNaN(d)) {
              return "('NaN'::double precision)";
            }
            return quoteAndCast(Double.toString(d), "double precision", standardConformingStrings);

          case Oid.NUMERIC:
            Number n = ByteConverter.numeric((byte[]) paramValue);
            if (n instanceof Double) {
              assert ((Double) n).isNaN();
              return "('NaN'::numeric)";
            }
            return n.toString();

          case Oid.UUID:
            String uuid =
                new UUIDArrayAssistant().buildElement((byte[]) paramValue, 0, 16).toString();
            return quoteAndCast(uuid, "uuid", standardConformingStrings);
        }
        return "?";
      } else {
        String param = paramValue.toString();
        int paramType = paramTypes[index];
        if (paramType == Oid.TIMESTAMP) {
          return quoteAndCast(param, "timestamp", standardConformingStrings);
        }
        return quoteAndCast(param, null, standardConformingStrings);
      }
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1564: the fixed revision routes every type through the wrapper"
  lang java
  file pgjdbc/src/main/java/org/postgresql/core/v3/SimpleParameterList.java
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  class SimpleParameterList {
    private Object[] paramValues;
    private int[] paramTypes;
    private int[] flags;
    private static final Object NULL_OBJECT = new Object();

    private static String quoteAndCast(String text, String type, boolean standardConformingStrings) {
      StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder((text.length() + 10) / 10 * 11);
      sb.append("('");
      sb.append(text);
      sb.append("'");
      if (type != null) {
        sb.append("::");
        sb.append(type);
      }
      sb.append(")");
      return sb.toString();
    }

    public String toString(int index, boolean standardConformingStrings) {
      --index;
      Object paramValue = paramValues[index];
      if (paramValue == null) {
        return "?";
      } else if (paramValue == NULL_OBJECT) {
        return "(NULL)";
      }
      String textValue;
      String type;
      if ((flags[index] & BINARY) == BINARY) {
        switch (paramTypes[index]) {
          case Oid.INT2:
            short s = ByteConverter.int2((byte[]) paramValue, 0);
            textValue = Short.toString(s);
            type = "int2";
            break;

          case Oid.INT4:
            int i = ByteConverter.int4((byte[]) paramValue, 0);
            textValue = Integer.toString(i);
            type = "int4";
            break;

          case Oid.INT8:
            long l = ByteConverter.int8((byte[]) paramValue, 0);
            textValue = Long.toString(l);
            type = "int8";
            break;

          case Oid.FLOAT8:
            double d = ByteConverter.float8((byte[]) paramValue, 0);
            if (Double.isNaN(d)) {
              return "('NaN'::double precision)";
            }
            textValue = Double.toString(d);
            type = "double precision";
            break;

          case Oid.NUMERIC:
            Number n = ByteConverter.numeric((byte[]) paramValue);
            if (n instanceof Double) {
              assert ((Double) n).isNaN();
              return "('NaN'::numeric)";
            }
            textValue = n.toString();
            type = "numeric";
            break;

          case Oid.UUID:
            textValue =
                new UUIDArrayAssistant().buildElement((byte[]) paramValue, 0, 16).toString();
            type = "uuid";
            break;

          default:
            return "?";
        }
      } else {
        textValue = paramValue.toString();
        int paramType = paramTypes[index];
        if (paramType == Oid.TIMESTAMP) {
          type = "timestamp";
        } else {
          type = null;
        }
      }
      return quoteAndCast(textValue, type, standardConformingStrings);
    }
  }
  ```

